            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Giuseppe Verdi's Early Life</strong><br>\nGiuseppe Verdi was born in 1813 near Parma, Italy. He grew up in a modest household, where he developed a passion for music early on. His talent was evident, and he began studying music in his youth, later attending the Milan Conservatory.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Fame</strong><br>\nVerdi's career took off with the success of his opera \"Nabucco\" in 1842. Its famous chorus \"Va, pensiero\" resonated with the Italian public, becoming a symbol of the Risorgimento, the movement for Italian unification.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Tragedy and Professional Triumphs</strong><br>\nThe early years of Verdi's career were marked by personal tragedy, with the deaths of his wife and children. However, he continued to compose, producing great operas like \"Rigoletto,\" \"Il Trovatore,\" and \"La Traviata\" in the 1850s.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
