          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Verdi's Middle Period</strong><br>\nDuring his middle period, Verdi's style evolved, and he started to incorporate more complex themes and structures into his works. Operas from this period include \"Simon Boccanegra\" and \"Un Ballo in Maschera.\"</p>\n\n<p><strong>Late Masterpieces</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Verdi composed some of his most profound works, including \"Aida,\" commissioned for the opening of the Suez Canal, and his Shakespearean operas \"Otello\" and \"Falstaff,\" which exhibited his musical maturity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Engagement</strong><br>\nVerdi was not only a composer but also an active participant in Italian politics. He served in the Italian Parliament and became an icon of national pride through his music and public service.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
